 business principles is that  execution is way more important than the  idea he says that everyone has a great  idea but very few people are able to  execute mark also preaches that  following your passion is one of the  great lies of life if he had followed  his passion he says that he would have  ended up as a field basketball or  baseball player  instead mark has always insisted on  following opportunity and the  opportunity with micro solutions was  that mark had already built up a client  base at his old job so he just had to  convince them to switch over and being  the hustler that he is this wasn't too  difficult  aside from building up a solid client  base including people like ross pro mark  was quick to adopt new technologies such  as remote screen sharing client server  software platforms and of course the  internet by 1990 micro solutions had  grown to 30 million revenue and this  stellar performance started to attract  some acquisition offers and that same  year mark would sell micro solutions to  compuserve for 6 million dollars which  worked out to about 2 million after  taxes for mark adjusting for inflation  we're talking about around 4.2 million  dollars which is nowhere close to being  a billionaire but mark was more than  happy with this amount you see mark was  never trying to become a billionaire he  just wanted to be financially free and  enjoy life and 4.2 million dollars was  more than enough to do just that one of  mark's first orders of business after  cashing out was spending six hundred  thousand dollars on an american airlines  unlimited pass as the name suggests this  allows mark to travel on american  airlines first class unlimited times  mark says that over the next five years  he used the pass to travel the world and  party like a madness so i bought that  lifetime pass on american airlines we'd  walk into a club and this was after i  sold my company and we just buy bottles  of cristal  for everybody apparently the long-term  cost o